  "question": {
    "text": "The change of entropy $(d S)$ is defined as"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$d S=\\frac{\\delta q}{T}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$d S=\\frac{d H}{T}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$d S=\\frac{\\delta q_{eqv}}{T}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$d S=\\frac{d H-d G}{T}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "The entropy is the measure of disorder or randomness in a system. When a system changes from one state to another, the change of entropy, $d S$ is given by\r\n$$\r\nd S=\\frac{\\delta q_{\\mathrm{rev}}}{T}\r\n$$"
  }
}